  set:  # bdc9
    priority: 2  # bdc9
    title: "BUG-06: --backend rust-analyzer and install-rust-analyzer are silent no-op surfaces in published v4.1.0 distribution (integration package missing)"  # bdc9
    description: "## Symptom\n\nThe published v4.1.0 hypergumbo distribution does not contain the Python integration package `hypergumbo-lang-rust-analyzer` for the documented `--backend rust-analyzer` SCIP backend. Both the `--backend rust-analyzer` flag and the `hypergumbo install-rust-analyzer` subcommand pass argparse and run without error, producing output that is observably indistinguishable from a default-backend run. No error, no warning, no log line — silent fall-through.\n\n## Repro (from hg-uat-v4.1.0 Round 10)\n\n```bash\n# Confirm the rustup component is installed (binary IS present):\nrustup component list --installed | grep rust-analyzer\n\n# Confirm the Python integration package is missing from the venv:\n~/.local/share/pipx/venvs/hypergumbo/bin/python -c \\\n  'import hypergumbo_lang_rust_analyzer'\n# → ModuleNotFoundError: No module named 'hypergumbo_lang_rust_analyzer'\n\n# Confirm distribution metadata doesn't reference the integration package:\n~/.local/share/pipx/venvs/hypergumbo/bin/python -c \\\n  \"from importlib.metadata import metadata; \\\n   print(metadata('hypergumbo').get_all('Requires-Dist'))\"\n# → only hypergumbo-core, hypergumbo-lang-{common,mainstream,extended1};\n#   no rust-analyzer integration\n\n# Confirm PyPI has no distribution under any plausible variant:\npipx inject hypergumbo hypergumbo-lang-rust-analyzer\n# → No matching distribution found\n```\n\n## Empirical observations (Round 10)\n\n- Three invocation variants on a 2-impl trait probe (`--backend rust-analyzer`; `HYPERGUMBO_RUST_ANALYZER=1`; both) all produce `analysis_runs` with **zero** SCIP-shaped passes.\n- Process-tree probe during a live run shows no `rust-analyzer` subprocess child of the hypergumbo Python process.\n- Round 09 (deprecated) misdiagnosed this as a flag-positioning issue. Round 10 placed the flag at the documented top-level position (`hypergumbo --backend rust-analyzer run …`) and observed the same null result, confirming the issue is independent of flag placement.\n\n## Severity rationale (MED–HIGH per master report)\n\n**Why MED–HIGH rather than HIGH:**\n- The default (tree-sitter) backend works correctly; no user gets silently-wrong results from this issue.\n- `hypergumbo install-rust-analyzer` does install the rustup binary successfully — that part isn't broken.\n- The breakage is a missing feature, not a corrupted feature.\n\n**Why not LOW:**\n- A documented public CLI surface is fully no-op. A user can spend hours wondering why `--backend rust-analyzer` runs aren't different from default runs.\n- Detecting the issue required process-tree + distribution-metadata probes; no surface signal alerts the user.\n- The issue led the orchestrator's own investigation astray (Round 09's 'Outcome (A)' verdict was vacuous; Round 10's first-draft diagnosis was off; both rounds had to be deprecated).\n\n## Suggested fix\n\n1. Publish `hypergumbo-lang-rust-analyzer` to PyPI and add it to `hypergumbo`'s `Requires-Dist` (or as a `rust-analyzer` extra). Then `pipx install 'hypergumbo[rust-analyzer]'` actually engages the SCIP backend.\n2. Until (1) lands, gate `--backend rust-analyzer` and `install-rust-analyzer` at runtime: detect the missing import and raise a clear error ('the rust-analyzer integration package is not installed; …') rather than silently falling through.\n\n## Acceptance\n\n- One of the two suggested fixes lands in v4.1.1 (or v4.2.0). Verifiable by either:\n  (a) installable via `pipx install 'hypergumbo[rust-analyzer]'` (or equivalent) and `--backend rust-analyzer` produces a SCIP-shaped pass in `analysis_runs`; OR\n  (b) `--backend rust-analyzer` raises a clear runtime error when the integration package is not installed.\n- Property test guards the chosen behavior so silent fall-through does not regress.\n\n## Carry-forward note\n\nOnce BUG-06 is fixed and the integration package is installable on the published distribution, the originally-planned investigation (does SCIP engagement change BUG-04's manifestation on candle?) becomes runnable. Until then, the producer-locus claim for BUG-04 stands by elimination of alternatives (rust-v1 is the only Rust-edge producer in v4.1.0) but is not empirically confirmed.\n\n## Secondary observation (separate latent issue, not the headline)\n\nIndependent of BUG-06: argparse accepts `hypergumbo run --backend rust-analyzer` (flag *after* the subcommand) without erroring, even though `--backend` is registered only at the top level (cli.py:4860). The expected behavior is one of: (a) argparse rejects with 'unrecognized arguments', or (b) `--backend` is plumbed through to subparsers. This was the orchestrator's initial hypothesis for Round 09's failure; Round 10 falsified it (the SCIP backend is structurally absent regardless of flag position). The argparse silent-accept is still a real UX issue worth fixing in a separate follow-up if it fragments user investigation again, but it is *not* the cause of Rounds 09–10's null results.\n\n## References\n\n- Round 10 (deprecated): `~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/bakeoff_artifacts/hg-uat-v4.1.0/lab-notebook/deprecated_rounds/round-10-rust-analyzer-backend-replication/`\n- Round 09 (deprecated, originally misdiagnosed): `~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/bakeoff_artifacts/hg-uat-v4.1.0/lab-notebook/deprecated_rounds/round-09-rust-analyzer-backend-replication/`\n- Master report §3 BUG-06: `~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/bakeoff_artifacts/hg-uat-v4.1.0/lab-notebook/master-report.md`\n- Top-level flag definition: `packages/hypergumbo-core/src/hypergumbo_core/cli.py:4860-4861`\n- Gate logic: `packages/hypergumbo-lang-rust-analyzer/src/hypergumbo_lang_rust_analyzer/gate.py:57-91`"  # bdc9
